On Sun, Jun 16, 2013 at 5:27 AM, la arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>wrote:

>
> {mi} or {za'u mi} has certain implications that "we" doesn't have.


Side issue:

"za'u mi" means "more than one of us", it is not the same as "mi noi za'u
mei".

Similarly, "pa mi" means "one of us", it does not mean "mi noi pa mei".

"pa mi" and "za'u mi" is not the right way to distinguish singular "mi"
from plural "mi".

mu'o mi'e xorxes

